,"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T23:37:49-07:00","id":1377669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1377667#post1377667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resources 6\u201310 (Hollywood money to Bill Gates level wealth; M20 top of p.323) doesn't work for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a good start. Fleshing out is always nice though. :P We've had the Syndicate Wealth rules for a while and various editions of the World of Darkness have touched upon it, I am just curious what a book dedicated to it will do to flesh it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T00:42:03-07:00","id":1377679,"title":"","content":"Anything above 5, I just started using something akin to what Adventure had, in this case Wealth Beyond Averice, where if something can be purchased, you can afford it. The logistics of taking possession may be a different hurdle, but at that point the character's wealth is a plot device rather than a mechanical trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:26:27-07:00","id":1378101,"title":"","content":"It's an idea Phil has wanted to do for a long time, it's something he floated in 2E. It's also what to do with ungodly amounts of wealth. At a certain level it starts buying Influence and other backgrounds, and lends itself to a very different style of game than most people can imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:31:04-07:00","id":1378107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1378101#post1378101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an idea Phil has wanted to do for a long time, it's something he floated in 2E. It's also what to do with ungodly amounts of wealth. At a certain level it starts buying Influence and other backgrounds, and lends itself to a very different style of game than most people can imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly why this is such a great idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T10:02:53-07:00","id":1379011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1377666#post1377666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A functional system to represent people that could if they wanted Buy a Submarine or Cruiseship every now and then, or build and staff a skyscraper. OR Folks if they liquidated all their assets it would put their field of business into turmoil. Supermoney!</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm with the rest of the thread inasmuch as, from a dots-on-page perspective, it's <i>mostly </i>just a matter of having higher resources.<br /> <br /> But while all you need to build or buy a cruise ship or skyscraper is money (and perfectly attainable permits and junk, and you probably want to have the cruise ship built in Norway for various practical and regulatory reasons), buying a submarine probably requires some more backgrounds. First off, what kind of sub do you want? Do you want the submarine yacht, a crude narco sub, or do you want a <i>bona fide </i>war vessel? If the latter, you're probably going to need some combination of backgrounds to reflect that you know the proper channels through which to purchase a submarine--probably Influence and Contacts at a minimum. The technocracy has merits and stuff as well that deal with &quot;Red Tape&quot;, which you may or may not need.<br /> <br /> The next thing to consider is the <i>kind </i>of full-blown war sub you want. Do you want some old school, half-century-old diesel electric thing more akin to what was being used in WWII, or do you want something more modern? Realize that no matter what direction you go, the purchase will be noted, tracked, and your activities closely followed <i>for the rest of time</i> by any and all intelligence service worth it's salt--<i>minimum</i>, the Five Eyes, China, Russia, and Israel. So even if you weren't on the Technocracy's radar before.<br /> <br /> As far the sliding scale of difficult, and amount of dots you need on the page to get different kinds of war subs, the low end would be the WWII- and thereabouts-era vessels, which you could probably buy one off of the dictator of some third-world country; other countries may try to block the sale, but it's not like you're necessarily an existential threat to anyone or shipping at that point since the capabilities of such an old boat can't really touch modern anti-submarine tactic and capabilities. The middle part of the scale are the very dangerous diesel-electrics that Russia will basically sell anyone (well, any country anyway), like Kilo-class subs. Based on what I've read, these things are pretty dangerous: whisper quiet running on batteries and traveling under 5 knots. The higher-end of the scale are the subs that you would necessarily <i>have </i>to steal (or bamboozle the hell out of someone to get): the newer UK diesel electrics that you would truly need to be in NATO to buy; any American sub; any nuclear-powered sub.<br /> <br /> If you're a hyper rich mage, I think you're probably be best off buying a Kilo or lesser, then using magic to make it better--or just steal some plans and make your own sub. If you want more systems to use as guidelines for the costs of constructing or heavily modifying a sub, I would use as my starting point the build-a-spaceship system found in the back of <i>Void Engineers (Rev.)</i>, which breaks down different vessels attributes (size, speed, etc.) and features into a point system, and then assigns a monetary sum to every point. For reference, the cooler/more badass Voidships come in around the mid-10-figures in USD based on this point-buy system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T02:59:41-07:00","id":1379193,"title":"","content":"Well Mage Wise if you have a crew of Mages, some at least millionaires, they can essentially cheat as far as obtaining a sub in that they can replicate lots of unrelocatable parts, steal technology so they can build things, and create materials so its untraceable. Not a super big deal since mages can also have spaceships.<br /> <br /> But there are things that get weird with high resources, they carry a weight were by definition your resources probably mean you have insane amount of employees, or you own shares that influence business in a manner that certainly effects employees. Its odd and having High Resources I would encourage other things like Influence and contacts to represent your money not just being in a giant Moneybin ala Scrooge McDuck. M20 also may have gone overboard with the extra Skills and Backgrounds, but maybe not, I like them but I know others don't like having things like a background to represent you are a doctor or to represent a pilot license.<br /> <br /> But the big thing I bring up is the Clan Lasombra own a submarine, one that is probably under the radar of everyone besides the Technocracy and other vampires. That does kind of set precedence of why not allowing PCs to get one.<br /> <br /> And what about being Billionaires so you can say I don't know buy an Island? Construct a Complex to link up a bunch of computers to make a supercomputer, lots of things that don't happen casually because they are insane investments.<br /> <br /> Resources past 3 start representing the capacity of employing exponentially more and more people. Its weird and complex. Who was it that was mentioning resources high enough will start becoming entangled with other backgrounds by definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T06:38:33-07:00","id":1379245,"title":"","content":"Since we are on submarines,<br /> I think your on the right path of it being far easier to steal plans (with magick) and secretly building your own than to buy one. I like the buying an island to use as a build site too. Man this gives me a new idea for a good little story line. \ud83d\ude08","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:31:06-07:00","id":1379335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1379193#post1379193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the big thing I bring up is the Clan Lasombra own a submarine, one that is probably under the radar of everyone besides the Technocracy and other vampires. That does kind of set precedence of why not allowing PCs to get one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you saying that the fact that Clan Lasombra has a sub is point <i>in favor</i> of letting PC's get a sub, or <i>against</i>?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:35:17-07:00","id":1379338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1379335#post1379335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are you saying that the fact that Clan Lasombra has a sub is point <i>in favor</i> of letting PC's get a sub, or <i>against</i>?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey definitely in favor, the Sabbat are Crazy Nobs, a saner wealthy vampire could get a sub with money and some schmuoozing with the Russian Soviet surplus that you know exists in the World of Darkness Ala Nick Cages Lords of War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T20:36:53-07:00","id":1379393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1379338#post1379338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey definitely in favor, the Sabbat are Crazy Nobs, a saner wealthy vampire could get a sub with money and some schmuoozing with the Russian Soviet surplus that you know exists in the World of Darkness Ala Nick Cages Lords of War.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hell, with the surplus that exists in <i>our</i> world. Ultimately, I could see a vampire (but particularly any vampire with Obfuscate 2) having a very nice life aboard a nuclear submarine. Bonus points if it's a high-dominate vampire who can basically just dominate the shit out of all the senior officers, or straight up possess the captain. Certainly we could say the Technocracy has surveillance devices or agents aboard every single nuclear sub in the world (there's aren't <i>that</i> many after all), but I think it depends on just how well organized and effective the Technocracy is in your game. My take on them has always been that they're far reaching and powerful, but either don't have their fingers in nearly as many pies as they want others to think, or have their fingers in all the pies, but are so overextended as a result that they have to pick and choose where they're really going to have their influence felt, and some stuff easily goes by the wayside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T20:44:08-07:00","id":1379394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1379393#post1379393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hell, with the surplus that exists in <i>our</i> world. Ultimately, I could see a vampire (but particularly any vampire with Obfuscate 2) having a very nice life aboard a nuclear submarine. Bonus points if it's a high-dominate vampire who can basically just dominate the shit out of all the senior officers, or straight up possess the captain. Certainly we could say the Technocracy has surveillance devices or agents aboard every single nuclear sub in the world (there's aren't <i>that</i> many after all), but I think it depends on just how well organized and effective the Technocracy is in your game. My take on them has always been that they're far reaching and powerful, but either don't have their fingers in nearly as many pies as they want others to think, or have their fingers in all the pies, but are so overextended as a result that they have to pick and choose where they're really going to have their influence felt, and some stuff easily goes by the wayside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah my sentiments as well. I figure a lot of resources go into obvious protections like making sure yahoos don't magic the Olympics or enslave the President, but even senators and governors I can see messed with, its just that they eventually do damage control, and you become a big target afterwards if you are the punk pulling that stuff.<br /> <br /> But I feel Submarines and Prisons would be prime herds for Vampires, to the point were Vampires often due use Prisons as supplies of blood, it would make an excellent research opportunity to hide a lab say under a prison. You can take easy blood go Downstairs spend it on your Thaumaturgy experiments or your Parabiology like Netchurch rinse and repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T21:14:20-07:00","id":1379400,"title":"","content":"In the Storyteller's Vault supplement Ascension's Landscape, it is mentioned that the rich and powerful (but I repeat myself) would be prime targets 4 supernatural powers that influence the mind. It also asks the question why the rich and powerful are not dominated by vampires and other Shadow folk. Hopefully, that will be one of the matters that this book addresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T21:27:27-07:00","id":1379403,"title":"","content":"Yeah I hope so too. My explanation works, but it only works based off of fear of consequences. You have ton of Nihilistic supernaturals. The Technocrats probably work on a few preventative measures so long distance Mental Manipulation aren't targeting certain key targets. They probably aren't blanket covers so while maybe the president won't be dominated by a sleeping Methuselah, Presencing a whole city into a bout of Mania would slip past it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T21:48:12-07:00","id":1379407,"title":"","content":"Ascension's Landscape suggests the possibility that the Technocracy has set up and is maintaining an ongoing countermagic effect that protects the rich and powerful from mind-altering supernatural powers \u2014 not by shielding them individually, but by setting up a blanket Effect that protects anyone who meets certain criteria. No game rules are given for this (the supplement avoids providing any crunch at all); but l could see implementing this along the lines of \u201canyone with six or more dots in Resources, Influence, or similar Backgrounds is under the protection of this Great Work and benefits from a die of countermagic against mind-altering supernatural powers for every dot in excess of 5 that they have\u201d. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that this is how I'd do it; but it's an intriguing possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T09:13:09-07:00","id":1379778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1377665#post1377665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you want in such a system?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Look at Lex Luthor and Tony Stark, and Bruce Wayne. A focused billionaire hating you is a monster foe. Also, billionaires tend to get their way in most situations. The truly rich are dangerous. And that can lead to drama and stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:13:12-07:00","id":1380268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1379778#post1379778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at Lex Luthor and Tony Stark, and Bruce Wayne. A focused billionaire hating you is a monster foe. Also, billionaires tend to get their way in most situations. The truly rich are dangerous. And that can lead to drama and stories.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel like the World of Darkness version of all three of those men is David Xanatos from <i>Gargoyles</i>. Dude is <i>practically</i> a Technomancer--he regularly cobbles together his own next-level tech; he dabbles in sorcery; he has all kinds of rando supernatural consors (guy married to a ninja heiress who is also a Fae princess); and he's a morally gray character. What's more, in that world, there is a flirting with the idea that science and magic are just two sides of the same coin when they explain the principle of energy being energy regardless of the methodology used to generate, harness, and directed it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T03:14:53-07:00","id":1380342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1380268#post1380268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like the World of Darkness version of all three of those men is David Xanatos from <i>Gargoyles</i>. Dude is <i>practically</i> a Technomancer--he regularly cobbles together his own next-level tech; he dabbles in sorcery; he has all kinds of rando supernatural consors (guy married to a ninja heiress who is also a Fae princess); and he's a morally gray character. What's more, in that world, there is a flirting with the idea that science and magic are just two sides of the same coin when they explain the principle of energy being energy regardless of the methodology used to generate, harness, and directed it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And such an iconic schemer that he has his very own tropes:<br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosGambit\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p.../XanatosGambit</a><br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosSpeedChess\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...atosSpeedChess</a><br /> <br /> He truely is the Rich Bastard","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T08:02:15-07:00","id":1380382,"title":"","content":"He's also a junior member of a worldwide conspiracy of know-it-alls who think they run the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:21:52-07:00","id":1380413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1380268#post1380268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like the World of Darkness version of all three of those men is David Xanatos from <i>Gargoyles</i>. Dude is <i>practically</i> a Technomancer--he regularly cobbles together his own next-level tech; he dabbles in sorcery; he has all kinds of rando supernatural consors (guy married to a ninja heiress who is also a Fae princess); and he's a morally gray character. What's more, in that world, there is a flirting with the idea that science and magic are just two sides of the same coin when they explain the principle of energy being energy regardless of the methodology used to generate, harness, and directed it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for reminding me. I gotta finish Gargoyles on Disney Plus. Such a great show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:58:33-07:00","id":1380418,"title":"","content":"Don't bother with the Goliath Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T01:01:40-07:00","id":1380596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1380413#post1380413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for reminding me. I gotta finish Gargoyles on Disney Plus. Such a great show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to quote you so you would know to look back at this thread, and in the name of all that is holy, heed <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>'s warning. I will second it. Do <u>not</u> watch The Goliath Chronicles, a/k/a Season 3. Your time would be better spent literally just starting at the wall in quiet contemplation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T01:14:18-07:00","id":1380597,"title":"","content":"Well\u2026 the first episode of it is fine. But after that, don't bother. In case you're curious, that first episode of the Goliath Chronicles was written by the same guy who was responsible for the first two seasons; but he had nothing to do with anything that came after it, aside from putting in a few suggestions that got butchered by the guys who replaced him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T06:05:53-07:00","id":1380635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377655-what-is-rich-bastard-s-guide-to-magic?p=1380268#post1380268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like the World of Darkness version of all three of those men is David Xanatos from <i>Gargoyles</i>. Dude is <i>practically</i> a Technomancer--he regularly cobbles together his own next-level tech; he dabbles in sorcery; he has all kinds of rando supernatural consors (guy married to a ninja heiress who is also a Fae princess); and he's a morally gray character. What's more, in that world, there is a flirting with the idea that science and magic are just two sides of the same coin when they explain the principle of energy being energy regardless of the methodology used to generate, harness, and directed it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Solid point. I'd also look at Ozymandyis (sic) from the Watchmen. Someone with scads of money, a genius intellect, and focus, is an awesome foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-13-2020, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}